From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:50:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] mmb: tiny-M kernel for BF16 weights with M <= 8 on RDNA4
 (GGML_CUDA_MMB_TINY_M_BF16=0: dense tile)

The warp-per-token tiny-M kernel gains a BF16-weight variant (four values per
8-byte load, widened to F32, the same F32 accumulation); its dispatch moves
into a shared launcher, unchanged for the F32 weight. BF16 dense weights with
M 1..8 that reach MMB (the shared-expert gate M=1, the BF16 hc inject M=4 of
a GSQ IQ3_S Flash-Next) take it instead of padding the 256-row dense tile, and
read the F32 activation rather than its bf16 rounding.

IQ3_S, 2 x R9700, one run each (off / on): smallpf 802 -> 826, pf31k 3903 ->
3898, midpf prompt 3054 -> 3070, needle prefill 3488 -> 3485 t/s. =0
reproduces the previous hashes; the production model (UD IQ4_XS) has no such
weight and every hash is identical either way.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmb.cu | 83 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 59 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmb.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmb.cu
